olab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":53},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791297821353,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":16,"user":{"displayName":"ÖMER ÇOLAK","userId":"16306115783918560316"}},"outputId":"76b9f112-8a15-47c0-a3eb-055c44721369"},"execution_count":41,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["\"\\nSquared deviations are 4, 0, 4, 0, sum = 8.\\npandas divides by N-1 = 3: sqrt(8/3) = 1.633.\\nnumpy divides by N = 4: sqrt(8/4) = 1.414.\\nSame data, different ddof. Our 4 readings are a sample, so I use N-1.\\nSEM = s / sqrt(N) = 1.633 / 2 = 0.816 C (N = 4, the lost reading doesn't count).\\n\""],"application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json":{"type":"string"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":41}],"source":["# TODO:prediction_std_pandas = 1.633\n","prediction_std_numpy = 1.414\n","prediction_sem = 0.816\n","\"\"\"\n","Squared deviations are 4, 0, 4, 0, sum = 8.\n","pandas divides by N-1 = 3: sqrt(8/3) = 1.633.\n","numpy divides by N = 4: sqrt(8/4) = 1.414.\n","Same data, different ddof. Our 4 readings are a sample, so I use N-1.\n","SEM = s / sqrt(N) = 1.633 / 2 = 0.816 C (N = 4, the lost reading doesn't count).\n","\"\"\""],"id":"c54"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"c55"},"source":["## Problem 7 · Look before you summarise\n","The notebook loads Anscombe's 44 points (F. J. Anscombe, *The American Statistician* 27, 17–21, 1973) into one DataFrame with columns `dataset`, `x`, `y`. Compute mean, variance and correlation per dataset with `groupby`, and a straight-line fit for each. Before plotting: do the four datasets follow the same law?"],"id":"c55"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"c56"},"source":["**Predict.** Same law for all four, or not? Say why. Write your prediction in the next cell *before* you run anything below. It is a variable, so it is saved with the notebook."],"id":"c56"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"c57"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["prediction = ...